      "assistant_text": "I\u0027ve successfully created the synthesis page [[concepts/single-composition-point]], but I\u0027m encountering formatting constraints with the index and log updates. The synthesis itself is preserved and answers your question clearly:\n\n---\n\n**Your credential-scoping and runtime-path decisions are two applications of the same underlying architectural principle: centralizing all critical configuration into a single composition point at startup.**\n\n[[credential-scoping]] keeps the Anthropic API key out of the Hub\u0027s environment \u2014 it\u0027s read and injected into agent child processes only at spawn time. [[runtime-paths]] does the same for file locations \u2014 all paths are resolved once at startup, then passed downstream as a validated set rather than rediscovered independently throughout the codebase.\n\nThe connection is that both patterns prevent **distributed, implicit initialization**. They eliminate the risk of credentials or paths leaking or being misconfigured, because there\u0027s exactly one place where each concern is set up. If you need to change credential scoping or add a new runtime location, you modify the composition point; if something fails, the failure happens in one responsible component, not silently in many places.\n\nThis pattern scales: as Grimoire adds new agents, new data directories, or new secrets, extending the single composition point is simpler and safer than threading configuration concerns throughout the codebase.",
